---
/**
 * MFL template install guide — the shared host's copy, at the ROOT.
 *
 * The successor to the 2017 "Project hawk" guide at mfl.football/instructions.html:
 * the same install steps (skin, CSS, homepage/header/footer messages, tabs),
 * rebuilt around the current header and footer. It belongs to no league, so it
 * lives at the root of the shared host like /brand, in the MFL app shell.
 *
 * The snippets are stored as files under src/data/mfl-template/ and imported
 * raw, so the code a commissioner copies here is the one saved copy — edit the
 * file, not this page.
 */
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';
import MflAppLayout from '../layouts/MflAppLayout.astro';
import { SHARED_APP_ORIGIN } from '../config/leagues';
import headerSnippet from '../data/mfl-template/header.html?raw';
import footerSnippet from '../data/mfl-template/footer.html?raw';
import homepageSnippet from '../data/mfl-template/homepage.html?raw';
import archiesHeader from '../data/mfl-template/examples/archies-header.html?raw';
import archiesFooter from '../data/mfl-template/examples/archies-footer.html?raw';

// SSR: the layout reads the theme cookie and the session.
export const prerender = false;

const cssFiles = [
	{ label: 'Dark', file: 'dark_main.css' },
	{ label: 'Dark (DIN headings)', file: 'dark_din_main.css' },
	{ label: 'Light — blue and green', file: 'roboto-blue-green.css' },
].map((c) => ({ ...c, url: new URL(`/assets/css/dist/${c.file}`, SHARED_APP_ORIGIN).href }));

// Icon ids are read from the same sprite the header loads, so the gallery can
// never list an icon the header cannot draw.
const spritePath = path.join(process.cwd(), 'public/assets/icons/sprite.svg');
const iconIds = [...fs.readFileSync(spritePath, 'utf-8').matchAll(/<symbol id="(icon-[^"]+)"/g)].map((m) => m[1]);
---

<MflAppLayout title="Template instructions — MFL" description="Install the mfl.football template on your MyFantasyLeague site: skin, CSS, homepage, header and footer.">
	<article class="tpl">
		<h1 class="tpl__title">Template instructions</h1>
		<p class="tpl__lede">
			A responsive template for your MyFantasyLeague site. It uses Home Page Messages (HPMs) for the
			header, footer and homepage, so every page stays fast on a phone.
		</p>

		<nav class="tpl__toc" aria-label="Steps">
			<ol>
				<li><a href="#before">Before you start</a></li>
				<li><a href="#skin">Skin</a></li>
				<li><a href="#css">CSS</a></li>
				<li><a href="#homepage">Homepage</a></li>
				<li><a href="#header">Header</a></li>
				<li><a href="#footer">Footer</a></li>
				<li><a href="#tabs">Tabs and modules</a></li>
				<li><a href="#icons">Icons</a></li>
			</ol>
		</nav>

		<section id="before" class="tpl__step">
			<h2>1. Before you start</h2>
			<p>
				Save any code you want to keep from your existing Home Page Messages, then delete them. Make
				sure none of them is already set as a header or footer — that interferes with the install.
			</p>
			<p>
				Log in as commissioner and open the <strong>Commissioner Setup</strong> page. On a fresh site the
				HPMs are numbered: header is #1, footer #2, homepage #3.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section id="skin" class="tpl__step">
			<h2>2. Skin</h2>
			<p>On the <strong>Select a skin</strong> page, choose <strong>None</strong>.</p>
		</section>

		<section id="css" class="tpl__step">
			<h2>3. CSS</h2>
			<p>
				Go to <strong>Images and Other URLs</strong> and paste one of these into the CSS URL field.
			</p>
			<ul class="tpl__css">
				{cssFiles.map((c) => (
					<li class="tpl__css-row">
						<span class="tpl__css-label">{c.label}</span>
						<code class="tpl__css-url">{c.url}</code>
						<button type="button" class="tpl__copy" data-copy={c.url}>Copy</button>
					</li>
				))}
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section id="homepage" class="tpl__step">
			<h2>4. Homepage</h2>
			<p>
				Paste this into an HPM and label it <strong>homepage</strong>. It lays out the homepage and loads
				the script that shows the log-in button — without it, owners can&rsquo;t log in.
			</p>
			<div class="tpl__code">
				<button type="button" class="tpl__copy" data-copy-target="snippet-homepage">Copy</button>
				<pre><code id="snippet-homepage">{homepageSnippet}</code></pre>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section id="header" class="tpl__step">
			<h2>5. Header</h2>
			<p>
				Paste this into an HPM, label it <strong>header</strong>, and set it to show in the header of all
				league pages.
			</p>
			<p>
				Replace <code>YOUR-LOGO-URL</code>, <code>YOUR-WORDMARK-URL</code> and
				<code>YOUR LEAGUE NAME</code> with your own. Everything written as <code>%HOST%</code>,
				<code>%YEAR%</code> or <code>%LEAGUEID%</code> is filled in by MFL, so the links follow your
				league from year to year — leave those as they are.
			</p>
			<p class="tpl__note">
				Keep the jQuery line. MFL&rsquo;s own page scripts rely on it to hide the left menu, open popups
				and build homepage tabs, and MFL doesn&rsquo;t load it for you.
			</p>
			<div class="tpl__code">
				<button type="button" class="tpl__copy" data-copy-target="snippet-header">Copy</button>
				<pre><code id="snippet-header">{headerSnippet}</code></pre>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section id="footer" class="tpl__step">
			<h2>6. Footer</h2>
			<p>
				Paste this into an HPM, label it <strong>footer</strong>, and check <strong>footer of all league
				pages</strong>. Its first two lines close the wrappers the header opens, so use the two together.
			</p>
			<p>
				Replace the champion link and icon and <code>YOUR-CONSTITUTION-URL</code>, or delete the lines
				you don&rsquo;t need.
			</p>
			<div class="tpl__code">
				<button type="button" class="tpl__copy" data-copy-target="snippet-footer">Copy</button>
				<pre><code id="snippet-footer">{footerSnippet}</code></pre>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section id="tabs" class="tpl__step">
			<h2>7. Tabs and modules</h2>
			<p>
				On the <strong>Homepage Modules and Tabs</strong> setup page, remove every module and tab. Only the
				main tab remains.
			</p>
			<p>
				On that same page, add one column at 100% and place the <strong>homepage</strong> HPM in it. Don&rsquo;t
				add other modules there — add them inside the homepage HPM instead, with a line like
				<code>&lt;module name="LEAGUE_CHAT" /&gt;</code>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section id="icons" class="tpl__step">
			<h2>8. Icons</h2>
			<p>
				To swap a nav icon, change the name in <code>xlink:href="#icon-…"</code> (and the matching
				<code>class</code>) to any of these.
			</p>
			<ul class="tpl__icons">
				{iconIds.map((id) => (
					<li class="tpl__icon">
						<svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href={`/assets/icons/sprite.svg#${id}`} /></svg>
						<button type="button" class="tpl__icon-name" data-copy={id} title="Copy icon name">{id}</button>
					</li>
				))}
			</ul>
		</section>

		<details class="tpl__example">
			<summary>Worked example: Archie&rsquo;s header and footer</summary>
			<p>The finished code from a live league, with its logos and champion filled in.</p>
			<div class="tpl__code">
				<button type="button" class="tpl__copy" data-copy-target="snippet-archies-header">Copy</button>
				<pre><code id="snippet-archies-header">{archiesHeader}</code></pre>
			</div>
			<div class="tpl__code">
				<button type="button" class="tpl__copy" data-copy-target="snippet-archies-footer">Copy</button>
				<pre><code id="snippet-archies-footer">{archiesFooter}</code></pre>
			</div>
		</details>
	</article>
</MflAppLayout>

<script>
	// One delegated listener, registered once when this module first runs.
	// `document` survives every ClientRouter swap, and the handler only reacts
	// to this page's own buttons, so nothing needs re-binding per navigation.
	async function copyText(text: string): Promise<boolean> {
		try {
			await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
			return true;
		} catch {
			return false;
		}
	}

	document.addEventListener('click', async (event) => {
		const btn = (event.target as Element | null)?.closest<HTMLButtonElement>('.tpl__copy, .tpl__icon-name');
		if (!btn) return;
		const targetId = btn.dataset.copyTarget;
		const text = targetId ? document.getElementById(targetId)?.textContent ?? '' : btn.dataset.copy ?? '';
		if (!text) return;
		const ok = await copyText(text);
		if (!btn.classList.contains('tpl__copy')) return;
		const original = btn.textContent;
		btn.textContent = ok ? 'Copied' : 'Press Ctrl+C';
		setTimeout(() => {
			btn.textContent = original;
		}, 1500);
	});
</script>

<style>
	.tpl {
		max-width: 52rem;
		margin: 0 auto;
		color: var(--page-text);
	}
	.tpl__title {
		margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
		font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 5vw, 2.2rem);
	}
	.tpl__lede {
		margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
	}
	.tpl__toc ol {
		columns: 2;
		column-gap: 2rem;
		margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}
	.tpl__toc li {
		padding: 0.15rem 0;
	}
	.tpl__toc a,
	.tpl__step a {
		color: var(--league-accent);
	}
	.tpl__step {
		padding: 1.25rem 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
		scroll-margin-top: 4rem;
	}
	.tpl__step h2 {
		margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
		font-size: 1.25rem;
	}
	.tpl__step p {
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
		line-height: 1.55;
	}
	.tpl__note {
		padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem;
		border-left: 3px solid var(--league-accent);
		background: var(--card-bg);
	}
	code {
		font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
		font-size: 0.85em;
	}
	.tpl__css {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
	}
	.tpl__css-row {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 11rem 1fr auto;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		padding: 0.5rem 0;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
	}
	.tpl__css-label {
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.tpl__css-url {
		overflow-wrap: anywhere;
	}
	.tpl__code {
		position: relative;
		margin-top: 0.75rem;
	}
	.tpl__code pre {
		max-height: 24rem;
		overflow: auto;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 2.75rem 1rem 1rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		background: var(--card-bg);
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		line-height: 1.45;
	}
	.tpl__copy {
		min-width: 4.5rem;
		min-height: 2.25rem;
		padding: 0.35rem 0.8rem;
		border: 0;
		border-radius: 0.4rem;
		background: var(--league-accent);
		color: #ffffff;
		font-weight: 600;
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	.tpl__code .tpl__copy {
		position: absolute;
		top: 0.5rem;
		right: 0.5rem;
	}
	.tpl__icons {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(6.5rem, 1fr));
		gap: 0.5rem;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}
	.tpl__icon {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.4rem;
		padding: 0.6rem 0.25rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
	}
	.tpl__icon svg {
		width: 2rem;
		height: 2rem;
		fill: currentColor;
	}
	.tpl__icon-name {
		border: 0;
		background: none;
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
		font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
		font-size: 0.72rem;
		overflow-wrap: anywhere;
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	.tpl__example {
		padding: 1.25rem 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
	}
	.tpl__example summary {
		font-weight: 600;
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	@media (max-width: 40rem) {
		.tpl__css-row {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
		}
		.tpl__icons {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
		}
		.tpl__css-url {
			grid-column: 1 / -1;
			grid-row: 2;
		}
	}
</style>
